n a couch in his office he had a  basketball game on  and he asked me this was a skit to come  in and call the game  so uh so letterman has you on his couch  and you're  watching a basketball game yeah yeah and  and then he tells me to cut it out  yeah it was it was david yeah so you're  doing play-by-play watching the game  with dave and dave doesn't want to hear  you do  exactly well actually you know that's  the way i started and my brothers alan  steen who also did nba games  we would turn down the sound of the tv  and do games on our tape recorder and my  son kenny did the same  with basketball and hockey and we had  our own  fictitious radio station uh  and uh it was great practice at the time  little did i know that i'd be doing  virtual  calls these days off the television set  you know so i was good good practice for  what's taking place now with both uh  tnt and espn great to talk to you have  fun during the post season  and uh please my give my best to heather  and uh thank you  thanks for joining us mark anytime dan  thank you i enjoy  listening and watching to watching you  all the time so  thanks so much that's uh marv albert  going to retire at the end of the  postseason

